From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:11:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 115/148] hjviewer: the tray tells when the PC cannot receive
 connections (UX-G2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-G2 (U42, decision D-18), Windows tray only, labels TR1-TR3 (critic 2-1):
- TR1: while hbbs refuses this PC the tray icon is res/tray-icon-warn.ico
  (the app icon with an orange dot at its lower right; the file comes from
  the overlay, client/icons/tray-warn-dot.svg through scripts/make-icons.sh).
- TR2: on a PC no login bound, in a build with the login, the menu has
  [로그인…] [이용 비밀번호 넣기…] / [Log in…] [Enter access password…] after
  [열기]. They open the main window with hjviewer://hjv-gate/login or
  .../password through run_me; the window's hjvHandleGateLink (wave 1)
  opens the login or P2. The links carry no value.
- TR3: a Windows notice (title HJViewer) once a refusal has lasted 60 s
  since the tray came up, then for each new refusal that lasts as long, at
  most once in 12 hours (a refusal within 12 hours of the last notice is
  told when they are up, if it still lasts); a bound PC is told to open
  HJViewer instead of to log in. Clicking it opens the main window as
  [열기] does.

hjviewer_access.rs decides (tray_now, tray_menu, tray_items, tray_link,
tray_notice, TrayNotice) and has the unit tests; tray.rs applies it in
HjvTray from three cfg(windows) hooks (built on every tray platform so a
Linux check compiles its tray and menu calls; the toast is Windows only).
No new IPC message, no bridge or FFI change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
